Let work outside any turn hold be-rust's runner (AsyncRunner::hold), so run_all_blocking waits for the tasks it will queue.
Upstream: not yet; to offer Kotlin Temper with patch 0010.

For std/net's requests on threads of their own (tempest's support.rs):
each holds the runner until its promise is settled, and
SingleThreadAsyncRunner waits, rather than returning, while any hold is
out. Runners that never return may ignore holds (the trait's defaults).

